# CLAUDE.md — VAMS release automation

This project is operated with the `vams-release-automation` skill. Before any
release work, read `skill/SKILL.md` and follow the workflow file it names in
`skill/workflows/`. The skill is the only source of behaviour rules; this file
adds Claude Code specifics and does not override it.

## Claude Code specifics

- Use the `vra` MCP server (`mcp__vra__*` tools) for every engine action. The
  `vra` CLI through Bash is the fallback for commands that have no tool
  (`vra setup`, `vra merge --abort`) or when the MCP server is not connected.
- Slash commands: `/vra-setup`, `/vra-watch`, `/vra-sync`, `/vra-deploy`,
  `/vra-promote`, `/vra-rollback`, `/vra-data-copy`, `/vra-resume`, `/vra-status`.
- Subagents: delegate conflict resolution to `vra-conflict-resolver`, failure
  classification to `vra-failure-triager`, the end-of-run summary to
  `vra-reporter`. `vra-release-operator` drives a whole workflow end to end.
- A Claude Code permission prompt is not a release approval. **[HUMAN]** steps
  in the skill still need the user's explicit answer in chat.
- In `claude -p` (headless) there is no human: stop at every **[HUMAN]** step
  and put the question in your final output.
